Thought: The user wants to see all repositories owned by the developer 'dev_user' on Github. The previous search used the keyword 'dev_user', which only returns repositories matching that keyword. To show ALL owned repositories, I should search with the search_scope set to 'owned' and no keywords, since the tool allows searching for all repositories in the specified scope when keywords are not provided. This will give a complete list of owned repositories.

Action: GitHubSearchRepositories
Action Input: {"search_scope": "owned"}

